  "body": "## What changed (step 1 of #692)\nThis adds one app-layer picking service. Step 2 (a separate PR) moves every UI picker and the MCP pick tools onto it. No picker uses it yet, so app behaviour is unchanged.\n\n### New modules\n- **`crates/app/src/pick/feature_graph.rs` (330):** the feature graph of a mesh.\n  - Welded faces are the existing `geometry::feature` patches, reused through `model::features_of_local`. `list_features` is unchanged.\n  - Feature edges are creases between welded faces, plus open boundary edges. Seams between the strips of a tessellated wall are filtered out.\n  - Feature points are corners (3 or more edges meet), turns over 30° and chain ends.\n  - The graph has a cap-8 cache keyed by the facets' digest.\n- **`crates/app/src/pick/feature_arc.rs` (90):** circle and arc centres of round feature-edge runs.\n- **`crates/app/src/pick/feature_pick.rs` (314):** the one pick API, `pick_feature(world, &PickQuery { ray, radius, kinds, through }, skip)`, with `pick_bodies` for world-free callers.\n  - It finds the front-most surface, then snaps point → centre → edge → face, only among the accepted kinds.\n  - Edges and points must be visible from the eye: a perspective view checks the sight line, an ortho view the parallel view line. `through = true` turns the occlusion check off.\n- **`pick.rs`:** registers the new modules; `ray_triangle` becomes `pub(crate)` so the new code shares it.\n\nThe thresholds and the alternatives dropped are in `docs/decisions/692-pick-graph.md`.\n\n## Tested\n**Pinned by `crates/app/tests/feature_pick.rs` (7/7):**\n- `flat_face_triangulation_edges_are_not_pickable`\n- `cylinder_facet_edges_are_not_pickable_but_its_rim_is`\n- `a_box_corner_is_a_point_but_a_vertex_inside_a_face_is_not`\n- `a_far_side_edge_is_not_picked_through_the_near_face` (perspective and ortho)\n- `pick_through_does_pick_the_far_side_edge` (perspective and ortho)\n- `the_world_pick_honours_placements`\n- `degenerate_input_picks_nothing_and_never_panics`\n\n**Also green:**\n- app lib 103, `pick` 9, `mcp_pick` 2, `mcp` 13, `face_origin` 3, `vertex_pick` 4, `plane_align` 8, `plane_align_edges` 5, `axis_align` 10, `wcs_align` 5, `feature` 18.\n- `cargo check -p camcraft-ui` passes.\n- Clippy `-D warnings` on the app lib and `feature_pick` is clean.\n\nThe full app test build still fails on main in `lathe_thread_travel` (#686, not this PR), so I ran the suites one by one.\n\n## Not exercised / left for step 2\n- **UI and MCP pickers:** none is rewired yet. The UI has to turn its pixel radius into mm at the hit and build the `PickRay` from its camera.\n- **Edges to chains:** an edge pick returns one edge, and the UI still maps it to a `FeatureSel::Chain`.\n- **Centres:** they need a `FeatureSel` variant before a mode can store one.\n- **Pick through:** there is no \"pick through\" toggle in the UI yet, and the user-docs note (#688) is still owed.\n- **Behaviour change in step 2:** once wired, rim vertices of round holes stop being pickable points, since they aren't feature points.\n\nChangelog: none (no user-visible change until step 2 wires it)\n\nRefs #692\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
